# Cloudflare Pages _redirects
#
# Trailing-slash normalisation only. Locale negotiation for `/` lives in
# functions/index.js — Cloudflare Pages `_redirects` supports only
# `from to [status]` and has no way to branch on a request header.
#
# This file previously carried 15 `/  /{locale}/  302  Language=xx` rules.
# `Language=` is Netlify syntax; Cloudflare discarded every one of those lines
# as malformed and served the final unconditional `/  /en/  302` to everyone,
# so a Portuguese visitor silently got the English page. Do not reintroduce
# conditional rules here — they will fail the same way, without an error.
#
# Order matters — first match wins.

# Pretty paths (no trailing slash) → with trailing slash
/en        /en/        301
/pt        /pt/        301
/fr        /fr/        301
/de        /de/        301
/uk        /uk/        301
